      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "A 50‑mile wooden flume, finished in 1879, carried lumber at speeds of up to 50 mph to the Sacramento Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/challenge_california",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town’s narrow‑gauge railroad, built in 1884, hauled logs from surrounding forests of sugar pine, ponderosa pine, and Douglas‑fir.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/challenge_california",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Challenge sits on a narrow ridge that separates the North Fork Yuba River canyon to the east from the South Fork Feather River canyon to the west.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
